1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:12,500
In order to better simulate clothing and adjust clothing details, you can select the range of detachment when detaching clothing.

2
00:00:12,500 --> 00:00:21,500
To activate the soft-select detachment, please open the simulation and select the move tool, then select the soft-select detachment option in the background right of the 3D window.

3
00:00:21,500 --> 00:00:25,000
Or you can press Shift E to activate this function.

4
00:00:25,000 --> 00:00:29,500
After activating the soft-select detachment function, a spring that is used to set attributes will pop up.

5
00:00:29,500 --> 00:00:32,000
The settings in this spring are divided into two parts.

6
00:00:32,000 --> 00:00:35,500
In the above options, you can see the settings for the detachment range.

7
00:00:35,500 --> 00:00:39,500
Here you can set the soft-select detachment type, range, and detachment degree.

8
00:00:39,500 --> 00:00:47,000
In the following options, we can set the measurement method of the soft-select range, whether it shows the range brush, whether it is used only in the selected version, and whether it shows the weight.

9
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:49,000
The range brush is randomly opened.

10
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:52,500
When you move the mouse, you will see two circles that indicate the soft-select.

11
00:00:52,500 --> 00:00:58,500
The outer circle indicates the range of soft selection, and the inner circle indicates the degree of detachment.

12
00:00:58,500 --> 00:01:02,500
Now we turn on the full weight display.

13
00:01:02,500 --> 00:01:07,500
When you turn on the full weight display, the soft-select part will show green.

14
00:01:07,500 --> 00:01:10,500
The soft-select type is divided into two types, the curve and the straight line.

15
00:01:10,500 --> 00:01:16,500
The function curve at the bottom indicates the strength of the soft-select with the degree of detachment changed from the center of the brush.

16
00:01:16,500 --> 00:01:21,500
In different soft-select types, the soft-select curve is different. In addition, the curve is also affected by the degree of detachment.

17
00:01:21,500 --> 00:01:27,500
Now let's set the soft-select range and the degree of detachment to the highest to see the difference between the two soft-select types.

18
00:01:28,500 --> 00:01:35,500
When we set it to the straight line type, the soft-select center range is very small.

19
00:01:35,500 --> 00:01:40,500
When we set it to the curve type, the soft-select center range is wider.

20
00:01:40,500 --> 00:01:48,500
Return all values to default settings.

21
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:56,500
There are two ways to measure the range, surface measurement and straight line measurement.

22
00:01:56,500 --> 00:02:03,500
When the measurement is set to surface, the soft-select will be applied to the surface of the version you click with the brush.

23
00:02:03,500 --> 00:02:11,500
Therefore, your choice will only affect the selected version.

24
00:02:11,500 --> 00:02:16,500
Press and hold the shift key to press to turn off the Kunden mode.

25
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:24,500
If the method of measuring the range is set to straight line, the soft-selection will be applied to all 3D space such as the back of the mouse.

26
00:02:24,500 --> 00:02:25,500
Press and hold the shift key to press to turn off the button.

27
00:02:25,500 --> 00:02:26,500
Press and hold the shift key to press to turn off the button.

28
00:02:26,500 --> 00:02:32,500
This measurement method is more suitable for soft selection of multi-layered clothing

29
00:02:32,500 --> 00:02:37,500
By clicking on the button that only works for selected panels, your soft selection will only work for selected panels

30
00:02:37,500 --> 00:02:40,500
Not affected by the range measurement method of selection

31
00:02:44,500 --> 00:02:49,500
This option is very effective for panels that are glued together after some simulation

32
00:02:49,500 --> 00:02:52,500
Thank you for watching, see you in the next video

33
00:02:56,500 --> 00:02:58,500
Thanks for watching

